@crew abara-rosa
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hi. Abara, Survey. The comics in the common room? Some of those are mine.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, {me}. You might be in the next one. Drawn kindly. Mostly.   #funny
- Hi, {me}. Scanner's free if you need it. I'm just labelling.
? tier>=friend
- Hey, {me}. I drew you. Holding a spanner. Looking heroic. Don't make it weird.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. New comic up. Three people laughed in front of it.
? mood:low
- Couldn't draw today. That's how I know it's a bad day.
== near
? habit:common-room
- The comics wall. Mine's the one with the lift that sulks.   #funny
? act:meal
- Our family stall on Valo did soup like this. Not as good. Don't tell Brennan.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- My family runs a market stall on Valo. I grew up shouting prices. Now I whisper.   #funny
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- My comics. Little squares of life aboard. People find themselves in them, and smile.
